# SCS weight sensitivity (generated by scs_sensitivity.py through robustness.py; do not edit by hand)

Components: `results/structural_scan_components.csv`. Selection rule: `balanced_maximin` (select_model.py). Supervised numbers are matched to the configuration each family selects under each weight setting.

Baseline weights {'wD': 1.0, 'wM': 1.0, 'wT': 0.8, 'wC': 0.3, 'wE': 0.05}: proposed rule KNeighborsClassifier (0.713426; runner-up CalibratedSVC); structural-only rule SGDClassifier; round-2 two-stage rule (held-out seed 13) CalibratedSVC.

## 500 joint draws

- Proposed rule (one-vs-rest families): KNeighborsClassifier 486, LogisticRegression 8, SGDClassifier 3, none (no family passes the floor) 2, CalibratedSVC 1
- Structural-only rule (one-vs-rest families): SGDClassifier 500
- Structural-only rule (Legacy kNN included): Legacy kNN 404, SGDClassifier 96
- Round-2 two-stage rule, matched inputs, held-out seed 13: KNeighborsClassifier 274, CalibratedSVC 123, LogisticRegression 98, SGDClassifier 5
- Proposed rule with Legacy kNN admitted (evaluation-only): Legacy kNN 469, KNeighborsClassifier 30, none (no family passes the floor) 1
- Floor-passing one-vs-rest families per draw (absolute floor 0.5, on a scale that moves with the weights): 0: 2, 1: 2, 2: 1, 7: 12, 8: 49, 9: 434
- Draws with all 9 families above the floor (434): proposed rule KNeighborsClassifier 433, CalibratedSVC 1

